Z||000000||wkayl||06-11-2000||01:12 AM||||What would cause a sulfer type smell after driving, then shutting off for about 10 min and then restarting?  It is on a 86GT with 94,000 miles.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||06-11-2000||02:33 AM||||Catalytic Converter.  might be going bad..||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||06-11-2000||08:39 AM||||It's the cat...dang, Standard's getting good at this stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ed||06-11-2000||12:59 PM||||Before you start replacing stuff try a different brand of gasoline.  They vary in their sulfur content.<P>Thanks to "Click and Clack." ||||reg||1
Z||000004||2M4 Dale||06-11-2000||07:02 PM||||wkayl, My Duke does the same. I really hope it's not the cat. I buy most of my gas at Marathon.<P>Maybe it's time for a good aftermarket exhaust system...and just lose the cat.||||reg||1
Z||000005||wkayl||06-11-2000||07:24 PM||||I am afrad it mighe be the cat.  It doesn't have as much power as my GT of the same year and the check engine light comes on just after you get up to highway speeds.  It has a new egr valve and egr tube is ok also.||||reg||1
Z||000006||88formula||06-11-2000||08:17 PM||||The sulfur smell means the catalytic converter is doing its job. If the smell is excessive than you may have a rich condition, which could be caused by a vacuum leak, exhaust leak before the O2 sensor, or a bad O2 sensor. There are many other causes of rich conditions, I just listed a few of the common one's.||||reg||1
Z||000007||MCordray||06-11-2000||10:31 PM||||I get the same smell when I do about 5 miles of highway driving. My cats relatively new (about two years old), but I think/thought it was going bad because of the smell. I'm pretty sure my '86 GT isn't running rich, nor do I have an exhaust leak. Any other ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cooter||06-11-2000||10:59 PM||||An overly lean condition makes a converter stink also. Check for the famous glowing exhaust manifolds when you notice the smell is the worst.||||reg||1
Z||000009||triker||06-12-2000||12:21 PM||||It's probably the cat but check out the battery also.  I noticed my 87GT smelled like rotten eggs when I stopped for gas on a trip a few years ago.  The battery was swelled up like a basket ball and looked ready to explode.  I've always done my own work on the cars I've had over the years but I didn't want anything to do with that sucker!  I have to give the station attendant credit for taking it out.  Even with what he charged me for a new battery I was happy to stand back and watch.||||reg||1
